/how-its-built     /safety    301!
/how-its-built/    /safety    301!

# /beta is a real page now, not a redirect. It used to bounce straight to
# TestFlight, but a redirect has no HTML for iMessage to read, so shared links
# previewed as the bare app icon. beta.html carries the OG card and holds the
# TestFlight link as a button. Rewrite (200), same as the pages above.
/beta       /beta.html       200
/beta/      /beta.html       200

# /go is a real page now, not a redirect to Apple. It used to be a 302 straight
# to the App Store, but a redirect carries no HTML, so iMessage and Slack had no
# card to read and invented one from an App Store screenshot. go/index.html holds
# the homepage's exact OG card and hands off to the store itself, three ways.
#
# Rewrites (200), same as the pages above, and for the same reason those exist:
# /go is the address printed on the QR code and it has no trailing slash. Left to
# Netlify's directory handling, a bare /go 301s to /go/ — measured on production,
# not guessed — and that hop is cached in the browser of every phone that ever
# scanned the code. Not acceptable for a URL on signage we cannot reprint.
#
# Both rules are FORCED (200!). The bang is load-bearing: a rule whose path
# collides with something that already exists in the publish directory is
# silently ignored by Netlify unless it is forced, and go/ is a real directory.
# Without the bang these two lines look correct, deploy clean, and do nothing.

# /card is /go under a second name, for the printed QR card only.
#
# Same destination, same doorway page, same Open Graph card — the only thing it
# changes is the path in the request log, so a card scan can be told apart from
# a scan of the cart-path signage in Netlify Analytics. Two rules, because a
# printed URL has no trailing slash and the bare form must not 301 to it.
#
# Rewrites, not a redirect to Apple, and FORCED for the same two reasons the /go
# rules above are: the App Store URL stays written in exactly one place
# (go/index.html), and an unforced rule colliding with the real go/ directory is
# ignored without complaint. If /card ever answers 301, the bang has gone missing.
#
# The QR artwork in brand-assets/qr/ still encodes /go. A /card QR is a new,
# separately versioned symbol — this rule is what it will point at.

# ONE LINK SYSTEM (2026-10-05). /go, /card, /rental and /f/<shop> are no longer rewrites here:
# netlify/functions/link.mjs owns those paths (its config.path), sends iPhones to the App Store
# with the source tagged, Android to /android, computers home, and counts each visit. The two
# forced /go and /card rewrites above were removed — a forced rule would win over the function.
# Link previews still get go/index.html's card (the function serves it to preview bots).
/android    /android.html    200
/android/   /android.html    200

